# S10.2D-R2 publication rotation root cause — 2026-09-05

## Observed failure

The single R1 cutover reached the versioned S10.2D publication-rotation
one-shot and exited with status 2. The privacy-safe journal evidence contains
the exact Application safe code `S9_WMS_CONTRACT_REQUIRED`.

## Proven root cause

The S9 runtime derives the trusted Telegram channel before executing the
selected action. For `https://wantmeseen.com`, `_trusted_public_channel`
requires a loaded S10 exposure contract. The S10.2D rotation unit supplied the
WMS copy and WMS public origin but omitted `--s10-contract`; therefore the
runtime deterministically stopped before opening a database connection or
entering `rotate_queued_publication_content`.

Publication rotation, migration 0029, the scheduler, queue state, content
inventory, clock and startup timing were not the cause. This is a Control
systemd argument/contract mismatch, not a transient readiness race.

## Red reproduction

The existing Application test proves that WMS origin without an S10 contract
raises `S9_WMS_CONTRACT_REQUIRED`. A new Control regression requires the
rotation unit to pair `--public-origin https://wantmeseen.com` with
`--s10-contract /etc/tu1nz/adult-commercial-s10-wms.json`; it fails against the
current canonical unit because that argument is absent.

## Minimal correction and risk

Add only the missing read-only contract argument to the existing one-shot
unit. Do not change Application code, queue logic, scheduler architecture,
health severity, timers, migration or content. The contract file is already
installed by the reviewed S10.2D controller and is already used by the WMS
runtime/health surface.

The risk is limited to the one-shot reading one additional root-owned public
JSON contract before using the existing database transaction. Existing unit
hardening and `AF_UNIX` restriction remain unchanged.

## Validation and rollback

The previously red Control regression must turn green; all Application and
Control tests, PostgreSQL 17/18 acceptance, syntax, secret scan, CI and
same-SHA review must remain green. A synthetic PostgreSQL acceptance must run
the exact target rotation command with the S10 contract and prove the queue
transition without sending a Telegram post.

Rollback is deletion of the single added argument through the normal Git
revert/merge path. No server installation or R2 cutover is allowed until the
fix is merged, CI green, synchronized, and a fresh backup is verified.

## Local test invocation note

An initial unchanged-Application test invocation omitted the repository's
required `PYTHONPATH=src` setting and therefore produced import errors before
test execution. The canonical CI workflow and README both require that import
path. This is a local command-environment error, not an Application regression;
the suite must be rerun with the repository-owned invocation before approval.

The corrected import-path run under the macOS system Python then stopped at
the absent local `psycopg` dependency. The repository's existing `.venv`
contains the reviewed dependency version (`psycopg` 3.3.4) and is the required
local interpreter for the final rerun. No global package installation or
Application change is warranted.
